WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.866 --> 00:00:02.902
JESSE: On Prime Crime.

00:00:07.072 --> 00:00:09.409
JESSE: Two deaths
bring new questions

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.077
for a family dynasty.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.578
WOMAN: A lot
of people respect them,

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:14.948
but there are some
people who fear them.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.116
JESSE: The evidence.

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:20.086
JESSE: The testimony.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.854
He was pacing back and forth

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:23.722
and he said:
"I got a bad feeling."

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.725
JESSE:
And the incredible moments.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:43.910 line:0%
Hey there, everybody.
I'm Jesse Weber

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.611 line:0%
and welcome to Prime Crime.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.347 line:0%
This is where we break down
the most high profile

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.683 line:0%
and memorable true crime cases.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.386
Our next story takes us
to South Carolina,

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:57.156
where controversy,
speculation and even death

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.592
surround one family.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:14.407
JESSE: South Carolina,
June 7, 2021, 10:07 p.m.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.480 line:0%
JESSE: Attorney Alex Murdaugh
tells the 911 dispatcher

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.182 line:0%
that his wife,
52-year-old Maggie,

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:25.785 line:0%
and son, 22-year-old Paul

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.487 line:0%
are shot dead
at their family property

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.256 line:0%
known as Moselle.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:37.062 line:0%
Paul and Maggie were
found down at the kennels.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.632
ANGENETTE: Paul had been
shot with a shotgun,

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.434
shot in the chest first,

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.070
the fatal injury
was to his head.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.540
Maggie meanwhile suffered
five gunshot wounds

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.977
from what they said
was a 300 blackout rifle.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.046
Using that type of ammunition.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.819
JESSE: But who
could've done this?

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.221
In order
to understand the murders

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:06.359
we have to understand a bit more
about the Murdaugh family.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.861
The Murdaugh family
has been prominent

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:13.432
in the low country of
South Carolina for a century.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.135
ANGENETTE: Three
generations of Murdaughs

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.439
prior to Alex Murdaugh
were solicitors,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.973
basically the prosecutors.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:23.642
They were basically
the face of law enforcement

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.112
in that community.
A lot of people respect them

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:29.448
and revere them, but there
are some people who fear them.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:33.085
JESSE: Controversy, rumors
and even death surrounded

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.955
the Murdaugh family,
such as the sudden demise

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:40.460
of their family housekeeper,
Gloria Satterfield in 2018.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:44.196
ERIC: According to what Alex
told the insurance adjuster,

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.232 line:0%
that his dogs greeted her
at the top of the step,

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.168 line:0%
which caused her
to fall backwards.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.971
And that's the only
known statement of that.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.906
JESSE: Then
there's the mysterious death

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.208
of 19-year-old Stephen Smith,

00:02:56.341 --> 00:02:59.678
found on a South Carolina
road in 2015.

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:01.814
The state troopers
who were on the scene

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:04.117
that morning didn't believe
this was a hit and run.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.384
ERIC: His shoes
would've been blown off,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.518
there would've been skid marks,

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.354
there would've been some debris.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.056
So I think it was
blunt-force trauma and I think

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.792
he was dumped off
in the middle of the road.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.060
ANGENETTE: He was
an openly gay teenager

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.197
and he had attended
high school there in Hampton

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.732
with Buster Murdaugh.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.201
Randy Murdaugh,
Alex Murdaugh's older brother,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.837
apparently reached out
to Sandy Smith,

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.440
the mother of Stephen, and said:
"I will offer to represent you".

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.576
And Sandy Smith
really didn't understand

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.345
why she would need any
representation at that point.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:38.884
ERIC: Alex and Randy, either one
or both, were on the scene.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.021
How would he know
to show up to an accident scene?

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.824 line:0%
Buster says that he had
nothing to do with his murder.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.358 line:0%
I'll take him at his word.

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:49.562
JESSE: But there's something
else from the Murdaugh past.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.299
Something from 2019
that Alex immediately

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:56.336
mentions to first
responder Sgt. Greene.

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:08.648
ANGENETTE: Paul Murdaugh
and his friends went out.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:12.718
They were in his father's boat,
there were people on the boat

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:16.188
who said: "Let me drive,
you've had too much to drink",

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.957
and, you know,
the reports we've heard

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:21.694
was that Paul said:
"No, this is my boat."

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:23.262
The boat then crashes.

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:26.031
That resulted
in the death of Mallory Beach.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:29.902
He was indicted on boating
while under the influence.

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.071
JESSE: Is it
possible Paul and Maggie

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:34.640
were murdered
by enemies of the family?

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:38.277
Fast forward almost
three months after the killings.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.815
911 receive another call
from Alex Murdaugh.

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.967
People start to think:
"Oh my God, like,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.437
"somebody is
out to kill this family."

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.575
JESSE: But
as you're about to see,

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.611
sometimes in cases

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:15.080
things aren't exactly
what they seem.

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:20.486
Days later, Alex Murdaugh comes
clean and says: "You know what?

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.321
"Some guy didn't shoot me.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:26.592
"I asked Curtis Eddie Smith,
this guy I know, to shoot me."

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.405
I wanted to commit
suicide or be assisted

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:42.541
in committing suicide,
so my son Buster

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:45.778
could get ten million dollars
from a life insurance policy.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:56.455
Alex Murdaugh admits: "I've had
an opioid addiction for years",

00:05:56.622 --> 00:06:00.059
and so he 'fesses up
and he's arrested for this.

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:02.395
JESSE: And when
investigators dig deeper,

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:04.596
they find that Alex Murdaugh

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.732
was not the man
that the community

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.000
thought him to be.

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:11.103
Indictments come out
for Alex. Charges for

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:14.740
a number of financial crimes,
tax evasion,

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.110
stealing from clients,
stealing from the law firm.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:20.446
JESSE: Alex Murdaugh
would eventually be charged

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.982
with over 90
financial-related crimes,

00:06:23.115 --> 00:06:26.285
including embezzlement,
money laundering and conspiracy.

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:28.787 line:0%
But what else
could he be hiding?

00:06:29.054 --> 00:06:33.292 line:0%
Could he in any way be behind
the killings of Maggie and Paul?

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:46.305 line:0%
(tense music)

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.909 line:0%
(tense music)

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.650
JESSE: On June 7th, 2021,

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.487
Maggie and Paul Murdaugh
are found shot to death

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.190
on their family property
in South Carolina.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.126
Maggie's husband and
Paul's father, Alex Murdaugh,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:11.664
calls 911 to report
discovering their bodies.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:17.803
JESSE: While Alex
initially appears

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:19.337
to be an innocent victim,

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.440
during the course
of the investigation

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:23.575
it's revealed
he had been stealing

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.344
from his law firm and clients

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:29.348
and orchestrated a suicide plot
to conduct insurance fraud.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:33.118
As he was criminally charged for
these alleged financial crimes,

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:36.655
the question became,
is he hiding something else?

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:40.259
Is it possible he was
behind the killings too?

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.534
JESSE: Through a series of
interviews with law enforcement,

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:51.938
Murdaugh lays out his activities
on the night of the murders.

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:12.258
JESSE: There are
some odd things, though,

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:13.792
about Alex Murdaugh.

00:08:13.992 --> 00:08:16.062
For instance,
the footage you're seeing

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:18.564
is from a Snapchat video
that was taken off of

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:21.634
Paul's phone earlier in
the night before the murders.

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:23.936
Now compare
that to what Murdaugh

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:27.440
is wearing later on in
the evening after the killings.

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:33.779 line:0%
No one knows what happened
to that blue shirt

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:36.515 line:0%
that Alex was wearing
in the Snapchat video.

00:08:36.715 --> 00:08:39.418
JESSE: And let's talk about
that timeline of the night.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.521
The Cellebrite analysis shows

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:47.292
that Maggie Murdaugh's phone
locked at 8:49 p.m.

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.695
So did Paul Murdaugh's phone.

00:08:49.861 --> 00:08:52.497
It doesn't appear
that either one of them

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:54.733
pick up their
cell phones again.

00:08:54.866 --> 00:08:56.569
JESSE: Based
on this cell phone data,

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.838
investigators believe
the killings happened

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:01.874
between 8:49 and 9:06 p.m.

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:05.077
And they also say someone,
possibly the killer,

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.846
was manipulating Maggie's
phone before throwing it

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.616
on the side of the road
where it's ultimately found.

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:13.552
After nearly
an hour of no activity,

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:17.156
Murdaugh's phone suddenly
records a flurry of steps

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:19.491
before he drives away
from the property.

00:09:19.691 --> 00:09:22.294
And, in fact, data
from Murdaugh's car

00:09:22.427 --> 00:09:24.763
not only shows him
driving past the location

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:28.400
where Maggie's phone was tossed,
but so much more.

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.869
ANGENETTE: The data also
shows that Alex Murdaugh

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:34.707
is at his mother's home
for about 15 to 20 minutes.

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:43.515
JESSE: And speaking of
questionable comments to police,

00:09:43.715 --> 00:09:47.486
there was this exchange that
had a lot of people talking.

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:53.859
You know it sounds like
"They did him so bad,"

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:56.595
but a lot of other people
thought he said:

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.864
"I did them so bad."

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:01.833
That would be...
tantamount to a confession.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.705
JESSE: However, let's go
back to Murdaugh's alibi.

00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:23.956
ANGENETTE: He
was with his family,

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:27.026
he took a nap,
then he goes to his mom's.

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:29.362
He said he had not
been at the kennels.

00:10:37.102 --> 00:10:38.770
JESSE: Late
in the investigation,

00:10:38.937 --> 00:10:40.773
authorities
find something hidden

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:45.611
on Paul's phone,
a video recorded at 8:44 p.m.,

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:49.315
approximately five minutes
before prosecutors say

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:51.316
Maggie and Paul were shot.

00:10:51.617 --> 00:10:55.187
A video that changes
this whole story.

00:11:16.441 --> 00:11:20.946
At 8:44 p.m., he told
law enforcement he was asleep,

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.984
so this totally blows up
his timeline and his alibi.

00:11:26.351 --> 00:11:29.221 line:0%
It was the single most
important piece of evidence.

00:11:29.354 --> 00:11:31.490
It's Paul speaking
from the grave.

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:36.028
JESSE: On July 14th, 2022,
Alex Murdaugh was

00:11:36.161 --> 00:11:38.363
officially indicted
for the murders of

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:40.465
Paul and Maggie Murdaugh.

00:11:40.765 --> 00:11:44.370 line:0%
Up next,
a trial unlike any other.

00:11:44.536 --> 00:11:45.871 line:0%
The gallery was packed.

00:11:46.004 --> 00:11:47.873 line:0%
People were lining up
at 2:00 in the morning

00:11:48.006 --> 00:11:49.942 line:0%
to make sure
that they got a spot.

00:11:50.342 --> 00:11:54.814 line:0%
(tense music)

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:58.417 line:0%
(tense music)

00:12:04.957 --> 00:12:08.794
JESSE: It's January 2023,
the start of the murder trial

00:12:08.927 --> 00:12:11.163
of Alex Murdaugh,
the once prominent

00:12:11.296 --> 00:12:14.533
South Carolina attorney
now accused of shooting to death

00:12:14.666 --> 00:12:17.636
his wife Maggie and son Paul
on their family property

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:19.771
back in June of 2021.

00:12:20.038 --> 00:12:22.874
The same man who was
separately charged with dozens

00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:25.577
of financial-related crimes
for stealing money

00:12:25.711 --> 00:12:28.246
from his law firm clients
and the government.

00:12:28.613 --> 00:12:30.949
This trial was
watched by the nation

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:34.586
as the prosecution
and the defense battled it out.

00:12:34.753 --> 00:12:38.090 line:0%
About 8:50 p.m.
and the defendant over there,

00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:40.925 line:0%
Alex Murdaugh,
took a 12-gauge shotgun

00:12:41.059 --> 00:12:42.194 line:0%
and shot him.

00:12:42.428 --> 00:12:47.599
Just moments later,
he picked a 300 blackout

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.969
and opened fire
on his wife Maggie.

00:12:51.136 --> 00:12:54.839
PROSECUTOR: Family weapons were
used to murder Maggie and Paul.

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:56.975
ANGENETTE: The murder weapons
were never found,

00:12:57.309 --> 00:13:01.547 line:0%
but the examiner
from SLED did say he believed

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:06.251 line:0%
the same 300 blackout rifle
that killed Maggie Murdaugh

00:13:06.551 --> 00:13:09.988
was likely the same
300 blackout rifle

00:13:10.121 --> 00:13:13.325
that had fired
300 blackout rounds

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:15.527
up by the house months prior.

00:13:15.727 --> 00:13:17.329
JESSE: Prosecutors
would present the case

00:13:17.462 --> 00:13:19.531
that Murdaugh had
the means and opportunity

00:13:19.665 --> 00:13:21.633
to kill his family
on their property.

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:24.603
They pinpointed his questionable
activities through phone

00:13:24.703 --> 00:13:27.272
and car data suggesting
he moved quickly to

00:13:27.405 --> 00:13:29.240
cover his tracks and alibi.

00:13:29.507 --> 00:13:31.610
But they also
argue that Murdaugh

00:13:31.743 --> 00:13:33.579
lied to investigators.

00:13:36.514 --> 00:13:38.483
How long did he stay
in the room with y'all?

00:13:38.817 --> 00:13:39.918
And I say y'all
for the record,

00:13:40.052 --> 00:13:41.220
you and Ms. Libby, I apologize.

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.788 line:0%
About 15 to 20 minutes.

00:13:42.921 --> 00:13:44.890 line:0%
- Twenty minutes.
JESSE: And prosecutors

00:13:45.023 --> 00:13:46.424
would also claim Murdaugh

00:13:46.558 --> 00:13:49.394
tried to influence
the accounts of key witnesses.

00:13:49.528 --> 00:13:51.830 line:0%
He was pacing
back and forth in the,

00:13:51.963 --> 00:13:54.366 line:0%
in the living room and he said:
"I got a bad feeling."

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.836
There was a video
that was out, and he said:

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.371
"You remember
the shirt I was wearing?

00:13:59.504 --> 00:14:01.139
That Vinny Vine shirt?"

00:14:01.773 --> 00:14:04.343
In my mind I was saying,
"I don't remember

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:08.513
a Vinny Vine's shirt,
it was the polo shirt."

00:14:08.646 --> 00:14:11.983
BLANCA: I didn't really know
whether he was trying to...

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:14.919
get me to say that that was
the shirt he was wearing.

00:14:15.053 --> 00:14:17.322
JESSE: Yet arguably
the state's strongest piece

00:14:17.456 --> 00:14:20.159
of evidence was
the infamous kennel video.

00:14:20.325 --> 00:14:22.695
The recording
taken off of Paul's phone

00:14:22.828 --> 00:14:25.397
that places Alex Murdaugh
at the crime scene

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:28.367
minutes before
Paul and Maggie were murdered.

00:14:31.202 --> 00:14:33.171
The one question that remained

00:14:33.305 --> 00:14:37.109
is why would Alex Murdaugh
kill his wife and son.

00:14:37.242 --> 00:14:40.412 line:0%
The motive was
he had financial pressure

00:14:40.545 --> 00:14:42.047 line:0%
bearing down on him

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.817
in June of 2021
from a number of sources.

00:14:46.084 --> 00:14:47.553
So now it was gonna come out,

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:50.922
most likely, that he had
stolen 3.5 million dollars.

00:14:51.156 --> 00:14:53.658
The law firm
confronted him on June 7,

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:55.828
the day of Paul
and Maggie's murders.

00:14:55.961 --> 00:15:00.532
And they said there's
792,000 dollars missing.

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:02.401 line:0%
I said: "I have reason
to believe

00:15:02.534 --> 00:15:05.037 line:0%
"that you received the
Ferris money directly to you

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.439 line:0%
"and you need to prove
to me that you did not."

00:15:07.639 --> 00:15:10.142
ERIC: The state
felt he needed to divert

00:15:10.275 --> 00:15:13.545
the attention away from
all these financial pressures.

00:15:13.812 --> 00:15:16.415
JESSE: And then,
there was the defense.

00:15:16.615 --> 00:15:19.117 line:0%
There's no direct evidence,
there's no eyewitness.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.154 line:0%
There's no camera,
there's no fingerprints,

00:15:22.287 --> 00:15:25.457 line:0%
there's no forensics
tying him to the crime. None!

00:15:25.691 --> 00:15:27.926 line:0%
There were a number of things
coming into this trial that

00:15:28.059 --> 00:15:30.462 line:0%
that seemed to be problematic
for the prosecution.

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:31.997
ATTORNEY:
There's no blood on him.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.832
They didn't find
any blood on him.

00:15:33.966 --> 00:15:38.103
JOE: What's the explanation
for not having blood on himself?

00:15:38.236 --> 00:15:39.938
This would've
been a bloody mess.

00:15:40.071 --> 00:15:42.474
JESSE: The defense also
argued that the state's theory

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:44.543
of the shooting could be off.

00:15:44.743 --> 00:15:46.712 line:0%
My opinion is
the totality of the evidence

00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:49.414 line:0%
is more suggestive
of a two-shooter scenario.

00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:52.250
TIMOTHY: Why would one shooter
bring two long rifles,

00:15:52.384 --> 00:15:54.452
two long weapons to the event?

00:15:54.586 --> 00:15:56.855
You can't handle
and shoot two of them.

00:15:57.055 --> 00:16:00.425
Whoever shot this shot
or the shot, well,

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:05.564 line:0%
first of all the (inaudible)
shot was 5.2 to 5.4.

00:16:05.697 --> 00:16:08.067 line:0%
MIKE: That is the most
likely explanation, yes.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:11.102
I think the defense
presented evidence

00:16:11.236 --> 00:16:13.872
to try to show
that Alex Murdaugh

00:16:14.105 --> 00:16:16.708
really didn't fit
the build of the person

00:16:16.842 --> 00:16:19.211
who committed the murders
because of the evidence

00:16:19.344 --> 00:16:21.013
we heard about trajectory.

00:16:21.146 --> 00:16:24.550
JESSE: They also suggested
this investigation was botched.

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:27.118
But there was
a body footprint near his

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:28.954 line:0%
that turned out to be
law enforcement, correct?

00:16:29.087 --> 00:16:30.255 line:0%
Yes.

00:16:30.388 --> 00:16:32.458
ATTORNEY: Is that
preservation of the scene

00:16:32.624 --> 00:16:34.993
that new standards require?

00:16:35.126 --> 00:16:36.695
MELINDA: Not exactly, no.

00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:39.063
Do we know what other evidence
they may have destroyed?

00:16:39.197 --> 00:16:40.232
I have no idea.

00:16:40.365 --> 00:16:41.700
That's right, we don't.

00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:44.969 line:0%
JESSE: When we come back
this whole trial changes

00:16:45.103 --> 00:16:47.805 line:0%
when one person decides
it's time for the jury

00:16:47.939 --> 00:16:49.808 line:0%
to hear his side of the story.

00:16:49.941 --> 00:16:52.410 line:0%
- JUDGE: What is your decision?
- I am going to testify,

00:16:52.544 --> 00:16:53.912 line:0%
I want to testify.

00:16:54.212 --> 00:16:58.617 line:0%
(tense music)

00:16:59.918 --> 00:17:02.287 line:0%
(tense music)

00:17:02.421 --> 00:17:06.858
The evidence will show
he killed Maggie and Paul.

00:17:07.058 --> 00:17:08.994
Here is the law.

00:17:09.394 --> 00:17:12.130
He didn't do it.

00:17:12.463 --> 00:17:15.600
JESSE: In early 2023,
the world watched

00:17:15.734 --> 00:17:18.270
the Alex Murdaugh
murder trial unfold.

00:17:18.403 --> 00:17:20.805
The once prominent
attorney now accused

00:17:20.939 --> 00:17:23.675
of shooting to death
his wife Maggie and son Paul

00:17:23.808 --> 00:17:26.277
by the dog kennels
on their family property.

00:17:26.478 --> 00:17:28.947
The prosecution presented
compelling evidence,

00:17:29.081 --> 00:17:31.850
such as video from
Paul's phone placing Murdaugh

00:17:31.984 --> 00:17:34.753
at the crime scene
minutes before the killings.

00:17:34.886 --> 00:17:36.688
They also suggested
that Murdaugh,

00:17:36.822 --> 00:17:38.857
a substance abuser and defendant

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:41.426
in separate
financial-related crime cases,

00:17:41.559 --> 00:17:44.729
of killing his family because
he was about to be exposed

00:17:44.863 --> 00:17:47.232
for stealing money
from his law firm and clients

00:17:47.365 --> 00:17:49.201
and the murders
would be a distraction

00:17:49.334 --> 00:17:50.702
and buy him some time.

00:17:50.902 --> 00:17:52.637
Well, there was one man
who wanted to set

00:17:52.771 --> 00:17:56.608
the record straight and
that was Alex Murdaugh himself.

00:17:56.908 --> 00:18:00.546 line:0%
Mr. Griffin, I didn't shoot
my wife or my son any time.

00:18:01.279 --> 00:18:02.847 line:0%
- Ever.
- JESSE: And that is

00:18:02.981 --> 00:18:04.382
when Alex Murdaugh

00:18:04.516 --> 00:18:06.117
shocked everyone.

00:18:06.284 --> 00:18:09.955
Mr. Murdaugh is
that you on the kennel video?

00:18:10.088 --> 00:18:11.389
It is.

00:18:11.656 --> 00:18:14.393
Were you in fact
at the kennels at 8:44 p.m.

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:16.695
- I was.
- Did you lie

00:18:16.828 --> 00:18:20.065
to SLED agent Owen
and deputy Laura Rutland?

00:18:20.432 --> 00:18:21.666
I did lie to them.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:24.836 line:0%
I don't think
Alex Murdaugh had any choice

00:18:24.969 --> 00:18:28.306 line:0%
but to take the stand
because of the kennel video.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:31.076
He had to explain why he lied.

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:35.447
As my addiction
evolved over time...

00:18:37.115 --> 00:18:39.751
I would get any
situations or circumstances

00:18:39.884 --> 00:18:41.853
where I would get paranoid.

00:18:41.986 --> 00:18:45.223 line:0%
He did really quite
well in my opinion.

00:18:45.356 --> 00:18:47.626 line:0%
I thought credible,
believable...

00:18:49.227 --> 00:18:50.928
showed appropriate emotion.

00:18:51.062 --> 00:18:52.397
JESSE: He even
seemingly admitted

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.765
to the financial crimes

00:18:53.899 --> 00:18:55.533
he was accused of perpetrating.

00:18:55.767 --> 00:18:58.703
I stole money
that was not my money.

00:18:59.137 --> 00:19:03.508
I misled people that I shouldn't
have misled, and I did wrong.

00:19:03.708 --> 00:19:05.310
He's a liar and he's a thief

00:19:05.443 --> 00:19:07.980
and he readily admitted
that on the stand.

00:19:08.247 --> 00:19:10.014
But he said, you know:
"I might be these things,

00:19:10.148 --> 00:19:12.283
"but I didn't
kill my wife and son".

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:14.719
JESSE: When Murdaugh says
he was at the crime scene

00:19:14.919 --> 00:19:17.355
he claims he left
right before the murders.

00:19:17.656 --> 00:19:20.592
However,
prosecutor Creighton Waters

00:19:20.726 --> 00:19:22.027
wasn't having it.

00:19:22.194 --> 00:19:23.761 line:0%
The reality is, Mr. Murdaugh,

00:19:23.895 --> 00:19:25.597 line:0%
is the reason why no one's ever

00:19:25.731 --> 00:19:28.900 line:0%
heard that before is because
you had to sit in this courtroom

00:19:29.033 --> 00:19:31.069 line:0%
and hear your family
and your friends

00:19:31.202 --> 00:19:33.338
one after the other come in
and testify that you were on

00:19:33.471 --> 00:19:36.508
that kennel video, so you,
like you've done so many times

00:19:36.641 --> 00:19:39.043
over the course of your life,
had to back up and make a

00:19:39.177 --> 00:19:41.046
new story that kind
of fit with the facts

00:19:41.179 --> 00:19:43.248
that can't be denied.
Isn't that true, sir?

00:19:43.381 --> 00:19:44.950
No, sir, that's not true.

00:19:45.083 --> 00:19:48.886 line:0%
Putting Alex on the stand
was the single dumbest move

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:54.226 line:0%
I've ever seen when you have
a guy that's an admitted liar.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.263
WOMAN: Indictment
for murder, guilty verdict.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:00.999
JAMES: There's a lot of evidence
that points towards Alex.

00:20:01.133 --> 00:20:03.001
He can't, you know,
deny that he was there

00:20:03.134 --> 00:20:05.970
at that point because there's
a video that places him there.

00:20:06.104 --> 00:20:08.106 line:0%
Somebody that couldn't speak,
somebody that couldn't be a

00:20:08.239 --> 00:20:09.741 line:0%
witness was able to

00:20:09.874 --> 00:20:12.544 line:0%
be a witness even
after they passed away.

00:20:12.744 --> 00:20:15.146
JAMES: I think that he's
good at being able to talk to

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:17.248
people and I think that
whenever he's convincing,

00:20:17.382 --> 00:20:18.850
he's convincing himself as well.

00:20:18.983 --> 00:20:21.119
And I think he's able
to do that because he often

00:20:21.252 --> 00:20:23.488
meshes the truth with a lie.

00:20:23.655 --> 00:20:27.959 line:0%
Mr. Murdaugh I sentence you,
in the murder of your wife

00:20:28.092 --> 00:20:31.863 line:0%
Maggie Murdaugh,
I sentence you for the term

00:20:31.996 --> 00:20:33.765
of the rest
of your natural life.

00:20:33.965 --> 00:20:37.269
For the murder of Paul Murdaugh,

00:20:37.903 --> 00:20:40.405
whom you probably loved so much,

00:20:41.106 --> 00:20:43.141
I sentence you to prison

00:20:43.542 --> 00:20:45.210
for murdering him

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.913
for the rest
of your natural life.

00:20:48.113 --> 00:20:51.082
JESSE: Alex Murdaugh's legal
team intends to appeal the case,

00:20:51.316 --> 00:20:53.585
but right after the trial ended,

00:20:53.819 --> 00:20:57.221
a new update surfaced
in the story of Stephen Smith,

00:20:57.455 --> 00:21:00.992
whose death fueled rumors
of a Murdaugh family connection.

00:21:01.226 --> 00:21:03.261
ERIC: I'd been asleep
and when I woke up,

00:21:03.394 --> 00:21:05.797
I saw that there were
three phone calls

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:09.601
from chief Mark Keel
and he said: "Well,

00:21:09.768 --> 00:21:11.269 line:0%
"I'm gonna communicate
to you now

00:21:11.403 --> 00:21:13.672 line:0%
"the state of South Carolina's
official position

00:21:13.805 --> 00:21:16.741 line:0%
"and that is
Stephen Smiths did not die

00:21:16.942 --> 00:21:21.279
"as a result of a vehicle
accident or collision.

00:21:21.513 --> 00:21:24.549
"He was, in fact,
the victim of a homicide

00:21:24.749 --> 00:21:27.085
"and we're committed
to finding out

00:21:27.218 --> 00:21:29.421
"who killed Stephen Smith."

00:21:29.955 --> 00:21:31.256 line:0%
At the time of this recording,

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:34.326 line:0%
the Alex Murdaugh
conversation is continuing.

00:21:34.459 --> 00:21:37.695 line:0%
There's still his appeal,
the Stephen Smith investigation,

00:21:37.829 --> 00:21:40.265
upcoming financial crimes cases.

00:21:40.666 --> 00:21:43.101
Look, there are many things
that could be said

00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:46.204
about Alex Murdaugh,
yet more than anything,

00:21:46.505 --> 00:21:49.607
he is just
another example of someone

00:21:49.807 --> 00:21:51.642
who is not above the law.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.245
That's all we have
for you here on Prime Crime.

00:21:54.479 --> 00:21:58.216
Thank you for joining us
and until next time, stay safe.

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:05.724
(tense music)

